job_description:
PJA is seeking an enthusiastic Engineering Geologist/Geotechnical Engineer to join our Ground Engineering and Contaminated Land Team, based in Birmingham.

We would also consider a senior engineer with similar credentials. 

The successful candidate will form part of a team of geologists, geotechnical specialists and geo-environmental consultants who pride themselves on being able to offer robust assessments relating to geotechnical considerations and soil and groundwater contamination. In conjunction with the wider engineering team at PJA, we provide a diverse range of services from preliminary due diligence assessments associated with land acquisitions, to the design and oversight of effective holistic ground solutions to enable the development of both brownfield and greenfield sites for a range of clients.  

The successful candidate should ideally have between 3 and 6 years’ relevant post-graduate experience and should be able to demonstrate a grounding in consultancy. A keenness to learn about all areas of geotechnical assessment, and an interest in geo-environmental engineering and their interface with land development is crucial.  

The responsibilities for this position are anticipated to include, but are not limited to the following:  

* Preparation of Phase 1 Desk Studies and completion of site walkovers;
* Design, procurement and monitoring of site investigations, including managing contractors;
* Soil sampling and logging in accordance with relevant standards.
* Gas and groundwater monitoring and sampling;
* Scheduling of chemical and geotechnical laboratory testing;
* Critically reviewing contractors’ factual data and reports;
* Preparation of Phase 2 geo-environmental interpretative reports;
* Preparation of geotechnical reports in accordance with CD622: Managing Geotechnical Risk
* Develop geotechnical ground models for use in design;
* Appraisal of potential ground engineering constraints;
* Preparation of preliminary foundation zoning plans;
* Providing input to earthworks specifications;
* Monitoring earthworks construction;
* Preparation of Earthworks Validation Reporting;
* Assisting with preparation of fee proposals for clients;
* Preparation of site-specific health and safety risk assessments for site work;

**The ideal candidate**

The ideal candidate should have experience in the use of ground investigation data management software such as Openground and have excellent MS Word and Excel skills. Some experience of AutoCAD and/or GIS software is also beneficial.  

The successful candidate will be required to prepare clear and concise technical reports and other written communications, and they should be able to demonstrate that they can achieve this to a high standard, while demonstrating good organisational skills and working to tight deadlines. Verbal communication is also of key importance, and the successful candidate will be able to confidently communicate with peers, mentor junior staff, and communicate with more senior colleagues, contractors and internal and external clients. Good commercial awareness is required to ensure work is undertaken within the time allowed and within budget, some project management experience would be beneficial. 

Applicants will ideally have membership of a professional organisation such as the Geological Society of London or the ICE and should be demonstrating an ongoing commitment to Continuing Professional Development and be working towards chartership.  

This is a permanent, full-time position based in our Birmingham office, however the candidate must have a willingness to regularly travel to and from sites around the UK for site work and meetings.  Occasional overnight travel may be required. 

**As a member of the PJA team, you can expect:** 

* An attractive and modern working environment with good accessibility by all modes of transport
* The opportunity to progress quickly within the firm
* A wide range of challenging projects
* Ongoing support, training and mentoring from senior professionals within the business with a real commitment from senior management towards personal and professional development

 **We also offer an attractive benefits package that includes:** 

* Competitive salary
* 25 Days annual leave plus the ability to purchase additional days
* Hybrid working arrangements
* Option to participate in the Company Share Ownership scheme
* Private healthcare
* Cycle to Work Scheme
* Techscheme
* Payment of professional subscription
* Membership of our group pension scheme
* Life Assurance

  **How to Apply** 

If you would like to be considered for a role with us, then please email your CV and a covering letter to **recruit@pja.co.uk**. Please ensure you state the role/grade you are applying for in the email subject.

We're looking for a commercially driven and relationship-focused sales professional to manage and grow an allocated portfolio of TPI (Third-Party Intermediary) accounts and Bespoke Half-Hourly opportunities. You'll take ownership of the full sales journey, from qualification and pricing through to negotiation, contracting and handover, delivering agreed acquisition, renewal, revenue and margin targets while providing a responsive, high-quality partner experience.

Working closely with Sales Operations, Commercial teams and Channel Development Managers, you'll play a key role in converting opportunities, strengthening partner relationships and identifying new growth and cross-sell opportunities. You'll bring strong opportunity management, commercial judgement and attention to detail, ensuring accurate forecasting, effective tender coordination and disciplined follow-up, while using partner and market insight to help continuously improve propositions, conversion and customer outcomes.

* Proven B2B sales, account management or opportunity conversion experience, with a track record of delivering sales objectives;
* Experience managing multiple opportunities, tenders and customer requirements to deadlines, with strong pipeline, forecasting and CRM management skills;
* Strong relationship-building, negotiation, communication and problem-solving skills, with experience working with third-party or intermediary partners;
* Good understanding of commercial sales processes, including pricing, margin, negotiation, contracting, credit and governance;
* Experience in the UK business-energy market, particularly TPI, Bespoke Half-Hourly or multisite sales, is desirable, with confident use of Salesforce or equivalent CRM and sales-reporting tools.

* **Global Impact:** With offices in the UK, US, and Australia, and plans for further expansion, you'll be part of a dynamic, globally-minded team, with opportunities to explore new markets and make a difference on a global scale.

* **Flexible Working:** Embrace the freedom to work from anywhere in the world for up to 30 days a year. We prioritize work-life balance, recognizing that your well-being matters.

* **Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion:** We celebrate our diverse culture and value individuals irrespective of background, disability, religion, gender identity, sexuality, or ethnicity. Join a team where diversity is not just welcomed but celebrated as a key driver of growth and innovation.

Hybrid working typically means 2 days in the office location listed on this advert and 3 days working at home each week. Some occasional travel to our other offices may be required.

Once we receive your application, it will be reviewed by a human - no bots here! The average process typically takes around 2-3 weeks, with 2 stages of video interviews using Teams. However, this can vary depending on the role. We may invite you for a face-to-face meeting or require only 1 video interview. If you have any questions or need support, our Recruitment Team is here to assist you.

*We're committed to making the application process easy and comfortable. Let us know how we can help you with any reasonable adjustments that can be tailored to your needs. At the bottom of each of our adverts you can find one of our recruitment teams' contact details. Please reach out so we can discuss with you further.*

Deskside Technician



Job ID#:

45525

Category:

DWS-Local Operations

Location:

London,  United Kingdom

Position Type:

Employee

Job Description

**This is a 4 months fixed term contract**

Working in a fast paced, constantly evolving environment, you will be responsible for providing a high level of customer service and hands-on support. This is a fantastic opportunity to join an ambitious company operating at the forefront of their industry, and play a key role in ensuring the successful delivery of a premium IT support service.

**Job responsibilities**

* Provide face-to-face IT support for users, ensuring timely and effective resolution of issues;
* Manage support queues using ServiceNow, maintaining efficient ticket handling and prioritization;
* Demonstrate the ability to multi-task, adhere to processes and procedures, and follow pre-established guidelines;
* Coordinate with third-party vendors to resolve hardware and software issues as required;
* Perform hardware installation, relocation, and de-installation tasks;
* Diagnose and resolve issues related to personal hardware, including PCs, laptops, printers, and scanners;
* Maintain, analyze, and troubleshoot end-user computing problems, both hardware and software-related;
* Test system and application changes and prepare scripts in MS Windows 11 and MS Office 365 environments;
* Conduct basic Microsoft 365 administration, including Entra ID and Intune management.
* Install and configure equipment, cables, outlets, and other hardware required for IMAC implementations;
* Manage Windows 11 software, patches, and updates using Intune and Autopilot;
* Provide support for AV rooms and conferences, utilizing software such as MS Teams and Zoom;
* Offer remote and onsite support to users in other locations within the country as needed.
* Troubleshoot and resolve issues with warehouse equipment, such as label printers and handheld scanners;
* Handle user onboarding and offboarding processes efficiently;
* Maintain and manage mobile devices using MDM via Intune;
* Lead asset refresh campaigns within the country, ensuring smooth execution;
* Keep CMDB records updated using ServiceNow;
* Coordinate and manage local IT projects as required.

Job Requirements

**Requirement's**

* A minimum of 5 years of experience in an IT support role;
* Proficiency in Windows 10/11 and MS Office 365 environments;
* Strong diagnostic skills for hardware issues, including PCs, laptops, and printers;
* ITIL certification is an advantage;
* Familiarity with ServiceNow is highly desirable;
* Knowledge of remote administrative tools in Windows 10/11 environments;
* Understanding of LAN, wireless, and VPN technologies for basic troubleshooting;
* Experience with Intune and Autopilot for device management;
* Working knowledge of Active Directory and MS Azure;
* Familiarity with network-connected printers and multifunctional devices;
* A willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies;
* Positive and proactive attitude with strong teamwork capabilities;
* Excellent communication skills and a focus on service delivery;
* Ability to manage stress and handle workloads effectively;
* Experience with Zebra devices is considered an advantage;
* Fluency in English is required.

The preceding job description had been designed to indicate the general nature and level of work performed by employees within this classification. It is not designed to contain or be interpreted as a comprehensive inventory of all duties and responsibilities required of employees assigned to this job.

**What****we offer**

* Competitive salary and benefits package;
* AFB bonus;
* Private health scheme including Private Medical, Dental, Optical and Holiday Travel;
* Extra vacation days;
* Opportunities to learn and develop: training programs;
* Personalized career path within the organization;
* Exposure to an international environment as part of a multicultural team spread across Europe.

**Work conditions**

* Working hours: 40 working hours per week
* Contract type: 4 months fixed term
* Working setup (hybrid, on site, remote): 100% onsite

**What's next**

It's best to apply today, because job postings can be taken down and we wouldn't want you to miss this opportunity. In case you need further information, just send us a message at recruitmentEMEA@stefanini.com and we'll be happy to assist!
